# The F4 root system, the forty-eight roots of the exceptional rank-four algebra, the full symmetry algebra of the mesh
# cell, modeled by the kernel. F4 has two orbits of roots, set apart by length. The twenty-four LONG roots are the vectors
# plus-or-minus e_i plus-or-minus e_j over the four axes, exactly the twenty-four D4 roots, the vertices of the 24-cell. The
# twenty-four SHORT roots are the eight unit axis vectors plus-or-minus e_i together with the sixteen half vectors
# one-half (plus-or-minus e1 plus-or-minus e2 plus-or-minus e3 plus-or-minus e4). Those twenty-four short roots are the
# vertices of the DUAL 24-cell. So F4 is the union of the 24-cell and its dual 24-cell, which is the reason the 24-cell is
# self-dual and the reason F4 is its full symmetry, the Weyl group of order one thousand one hundred fifty-two. The antipode
# pairs the forty-eight roots into twenty-four opposite lines. The two lengths give two orbits of twenty-four roots each,
# each one closed under the antipode. This file constructs the roots, the antipode, the length classification, and the
# positive system, and proves the laws that make them a root system: the antipode is an involution, it preserves length so
# the long and short orbits are each closed, every root or its antipode is positive, and both orbits are non-empty.

load @term/seed/atom/flag
  find flag
  find either

# The forty-eight roots of F4 in three families. The LONG family is the twenty-four D4 roots, named by an axis pair (the two
# nonzero coordinates) and a sign pattern, p for plus and m for minus, on the lower axis then the higher: long-e12-pm is
# e1 minus e2. The SHORT family splits in two. The AXIS roots are the eight unit vectors, axis-e1-p is plus e1, axis-e3-m is
# minus e3. The HALF roots are the sixteen vectors one-half (plus-or-minus e1 plus-or-minus e2 plus-or-minus e3
# plus-or-minus e4), named by a sign pattern on all four axes: half-pmpm is one-half (e1 minus e2 plus e3 minus e4).
form f4-root
  case long-e12-pp
  case long-e12-pm
  case long-e12-mp
  case long-e12-mm
  case long-e13-pp
  case long-e13-pm
  case long-e13-mp
  case long-e13-mm
  case long-e14-pp
  case long-e14-pm
  case long-e14-mp
  case long-e14-mm
  case long-e23-pp
  case long-e23-pm
  case long-e23-mp
  case long-e23-mm
  case long-e24-pp
  case long-e24-pm
  case long-e24-mp
  case long-e24-mm
  case long-e34-pp
  case long-e34-pm
  case long-e34-mp
  case long-e34-mm
  case axis-e1-p
  case axis-e1-m
  case axis-e2-p
  case axis-e2-m
  case axis-e3-p
  case axis-e3-m
  case axis-e4-p
  case axis-e4-m
  case half-pppp
  case half-pppm
  case half-ppmp
  case half-ppmm
  case half-pmpp
  case half-pmpm
  case half-pmmp
  case half-pmmm
  case half-mppp
  case half-mppm
  case half-mpmp
  case half-mpmm
  case half-mmpp
  case half-mmpm
  case half-mmmp
  case half-mmmm

# TEMPLATE: one entry of a single-valued map out of a root, `from` sent to the construction `to`. One definition serves the
# antipode, the length test, and the positive-system test, so each map reads as its permutation or value table.
tree map-root
  take from
  take to

  hook fuse
    case {from}
      send back
        make {to}

# The antipode: negate a root, the point reflection through the origin. It flips every sign, carrying each long root to the
# opposite long root, each axis root to the opposite axis root, and each half root to the half root with all four signs
# flipped. So it pairs the forty-eight roots into twenty-four opposite lines, and each length orbit maps onto itself.
task negate
  take r, like f4-root
  like f4-root
  fork case, read r
    fuse map-root, long-e12-pp, long-e12-mm
    fuse map-root, long-e12-pm, long-e12-mp
    fuse map-root, long-e12-mp, long-e12-pm
    fuse map-root, long-e12-mm, long-e12-pp
    fuse map-root, long-e13-pp, long-e13-mm
    fuse map-root, long-e13-pm, long-e13-mp
    fuse map-root, long-e13-mp, long-e13-pm
    fuse map-root, long-e13-mm, long-e13-pp
    fuse map-root, long-e14-pp, long-e14-mm
    fuse map-root, long-e14-pm, long-e14-mp
    fuse map-root, long-e14-mp, long-e14-pm
    fuse map-root, long-e14-mm, long-e14-pp
    fuse map-root, long-e23-pp, long-e23-mm
    fuse map-root, long-e23-pm, long-e23-mp
    fuse map-root, long-e23-mp, long-e23-pm
    fuse map-root, long-e23-mm, long-e23-pp
    fuse map-root, long-e24-pp, long-e24-mm
    fuse map-root, long-e24-pm, long-e24-mp
    fuse map-root, long-e24-mp, long-e24-pm
    fuse map-root, long-e24-mm, long-e24-pp
    fuse map-root, long-e34-pp, long-e34-mm
    fuse map-root, long-e34-pm, long-e34-mp
    fuse map-root, long-e34-mp, long-e34-pm
    fuse map-root, long-e34-mm, long-e34-pp
    fuse map-root, axis-e1-p, axis-e1-m
    fuse map-root, axis-e1-m, axis-e1-p
    fuse map-root, axis-e2-p, axis-e2-m
    fuse map-root, axis-e2-m, axis-e2-p
    fuse map-root, axis-e3-p, axis-e3-m
    fuse map-root, axis-e3-m, axis-e3-p
    fuse map-root, axis-e4-p, axis-e4-m
    fuse map-root, axis-e4-m, axis-e4-p
    fuse map-root, half-pppp, half-mmmm
    fuse map-root, half-pppm, half-mmmp
    fuse map-root, half-ppmp, half-mmpm
    fuse map-root, half-ppmm, half-mmpp
    fuse map-root, half-pmpp, half-mpmm
    fuse map-root, half-pmpm, half-mpmp
    fuse map-root, half-pmmp, half-mppm
    fuse map-root, half-pmmm, half-mppp
    fuse map-root, half-mppp, half-pmmm
    fuse map-root, half-mppm, half-pmmp
    fuse map-root, half-mpmp, half-pmpm
    fuse map-root, half-mpmm, half-pmpp
    fuse map-root, half-mmpp, half-ppmm
    fuse map-root, half-mmpm, half-ppmp
    fuse map-root, half-mmmp, half-pppm
    fuse map-root, half-mmmm, half-pppp

# The length classification: yes for a LONG root, no for a SHORT root. The twenty-four long roots have squared length two,
# the twenty-four short roots have squared length one. This flag names the two orbits, each of size twenty-four, and the
# proof below shows the antipode preserves it, so each orbit is closed under negation.
task is-long
  take r, like f4-root
  like flag
  fork case, read r
    fuse map-root, long-e12-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e12-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e12-mp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e12-mm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e13-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e13-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e13-mp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e13-mm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e14-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e14-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e14-mp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e14-mm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e23-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e23-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e23-mp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e23-mm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e24-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e24-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e24-mp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e24-mm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e34-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e34-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e34-mp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e34-mm, yes
    fuse map-root, axis-e1-p, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e1-m, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e2-p, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e2-m, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e3-p, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e3-m, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e4-p, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e4-m, no
    fuse map-root, half-pppp, no
    fuse map-root, half-pppm, no
    fuse map-root, half-ppmp, no
    fuse map-root, half-ppmm, no
    fuse map-root, half-pmpp, no
    fuse map-root, half-pmpm, no
    fuse map-root, half-pmmp, no
    fuse map-root, half-pmmm, no
    fuse map-root, half-mppp, no
    fuse map-root, half-mppm, no
    fuse map-root, half-mpmp, no
    fuse map-root, half-mpmm, no
    fuse map-root, half-mmpp, no
    fuse map-root, half-mmpm, no
    fuse map-root, half-mmmp, no
    fuse map-root, half-mmmm, no

# The positive system: a root is positive when its first nonzero coordinate is plus. For a long root that is the sign of the
# lower axis. For an axis root it is the lone sign. For a half root, all four coordinates are nonzero, so it is the sign of
# the first axis, the leading letter of the pattern. Twenty-four roots are positive and twenty-four negative, the antipode
# of each positive root.
task is-positive
  take r, like f4-root
  like flag
  fork case, read r
    fuse map-root, long-e12-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e12-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e12-mp, no
    fuse map-root, long-e12-mm, no
    fuse map-root, long-e13-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e13-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e13-mp, no
    fuse map-root, long-e13-mm, no
    fuse map-root, long-e14-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e14-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e14-mp, no
    fuse map-root, long-e14-mm, no
    fuse map-root, long-e23-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e23-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e23-mp, no
    fuse map-root, long-e23-mm, no
    fuse map-root, long-e24-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e24-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e24-mp, no
    fuse map-root, long-e24-mm, no
    fuse map-root, long-e34-pp, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e34-pm, yes
    fuse map-root, long-e34-mp, no
    fuse map-root, long-e34-mm, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e1-p, yes
    fuse map-root, axis-e1-m, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e2-p, yes
    fuse map-root, axis-e2-m, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e3-p, yes
    fuse map-root, axis-e3-m, no
    fuse map-root, axis-e4-p, yes
    fuse map-root, axis-e4-m, no
    fuse map-root, half-pppp, yes
    fuse map-root, half-pppm, yes
    fuse map-root, half-ppmp, yes
    fuse map-root, half-ppmm, yes
    fuse map-root, half-pmpp, yes
    fuse map-root, half-pmpm, yes
    fuse map-root, half-pmmp, yes
    fuse map-root, half-pmmm, yes
    fuse map-root, half-mppp, no
    fuse map-root, half-mppm, no
    fuse map-root, half-mpmp, no
    fuse map-root, half-mpmm, no
    fuse map-root, half-mmpp, no
    fuse map-root, half-mmpm, no
    fuse map-root, half-mmmp, no
    fuse map-root, half-mmmm, no

# THE ANTIPODE IS AN INVOLUTION: negate (negate r) = r. The root set is symmetric about the origin, so the forty-eight roots
# really do split into twenty-four opposite lines. Proved over all forty-eight roots.
rule negate-is-an-involution
  mark r, like f4-root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call negate, read r
        link negate
      read r
  fold r

# THE ANTIPODE PRESERVES LENGTH: is-long (negate r) = is-long r, for every root. The antipode of a long root is long and the
# antipode of a short root is short, so the long orbit and the short orbit, each of twenty-four roots, are each CLOSED under
# negation. This is what lets the two orbits be the 24-cell and its dual 24-cell, swapped into themselves by the antipode.
rule negate-preserves-length
  mark r, like f4-root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call negate, read r
        link is-long
      call is-long
        read r
  fold r

# EVERY ROOT OR ITS ANTIPODE IS POSITIVE: either (is-positive r) (is-positive (negate r)) = yes, for every root. This is what
# splits the forty-eight roots into the twenty-four positive roots and their twenty-four antipodes, the twenty-four lines.
rule every-root-or-its-antipode-is-positive
  mark r, like f4-root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call either
        call is-positive
          read r
        call negate, read r
          link is-positive
      make yes
  fold r

# BOTH ORBITS ARE NON-EMPTY AND DISTINCT: a long root tests long and a short root tests short, so the two orbits of the
# classification really are both inhabited and the long and short lengths genuinely differ. A concrete witness for each.
rule a-long-root-is-long
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call is-long
        make long-e12-pp
      make yes
  calm hold

rule a-short-root-is-short
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call is-long
        make half-pppp
      make no
  calm hold
